.L18860:
    .string "(Secret T)"
.L18861:
    .string "Secret capability. A secret may not steer control flow, index memory, divide, print, spawn, send or be written to a file, and reaches FFI only through `ffi-pin`. Leave it with `declassify`, `ct-eq-bool` or `ct-eq-words-bool`."
.L18862:
    .string "let-mut"
.L18863:
    .string "special-form"
.L18864:
    .string "(let-mut name value)"
.L18865:
    .string "The only assignable binding: `set!` rebinds it, and every other binding is immutable and shared. There is no TCap/TMut type -- `set!` on a plain `let` is E_MUT_CONFLICT."
.L18866:
    .string "Secret"
.L18867:
    .string "capability"
.L18868:
    .string "(Secret T)"
.L18869:
    .string "Marks a value the compiler holds to obligations: E_SECRET_DEBUG, and E_ZEROIZE_MISSING unless the value is zeroized or passed on as a Secret."
.L18870:
    .string "declassify"
.L18871:
    .string "builtin"
.L18872:
    .string "(declassify value)"
.L18873:
    .string "Deliberately drop the Secret capability. The one explicit escape hatch; every use is a decision worth a comment."
.L18875:
    .string "Stack"
.L18876:
    .string "region"
.L18877:
    .string "Stack"
.L18878:
    .string "The call's frame region, released on return. A Stack value that would escape is E_REGION_ESCAPE."
.L18879:
    .string "Heap"
.L18880:
    .string "region"
.L18881:
    .string "Heap"
.L18882:
    .string "The process heap: values that escape every frame live here until exit."
.L18883:
